# The turn is the sensor daemon's own orientation event, sent by hwinput to its subscribers (T-653): LunaSysMgr turns
# the card as for a hand. The daemon's geometry line is the page's new window; the frames are kept for the eye.
# Back upright the only geometry line is the width's (win=768x686, the height follows without one): the content
# check down to row 900 is what proves the tall window.
id: rotate
section: Scrolling and gestures
item: Rotate the TouchPad: portrait ↔ landscape redraws the page right (both landscapes and back; the page's window follows each turn and takes a drag afterwards)
shells: enyo mochi mojo
page: http://192.168.1.245:8077/jihad-long-static.html
kit: cavekit-device-build.md R4
calibrate 'sel:#content p'
turn left
wait line 'emitGeometry.* win=1024x' 12
wait content 0,150,756,900 8
shoot landscape-left
turn up
wait line 'emitGeometry.* win=768x' 12
wait content 0,150,756,900 8
turn right
wait line 'emitGeometry.* win=1024x' 12
wait content 0,150,756,900 8
shoot landscape-right
turn up
wait line 'emitGeometry.* win=768x' 12
wait settled
expect content 0,150,756,600 'sel:body'
drag 480 900 480 250
expect card-scroll-min 400
